      "text": "PUNCH CONTEXT:\n  Colonial taverns: large communal bowl, served in cups\n  Social drinking before individualized cocktails\n  Ships: arrack punch (Batavia Arrack from Java -- precursor to modern cocktails)\n  Officers' mess: punch bowl as status symbol\n  Ladle served to guests from communal vessel\n  First punch: India (likely 1630s British East India Company)\n    -> From Hindi \"panch\" = five (elements theory)\n    -> Or from Sanskrit \"pañca\" = five"
